<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>BigSpeak Audio Health Dashboard</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<P><STRONG><FONT size=4>BigSpeak&nbsp;Audio Health Dashboard </FONT></STRONG></P><SPAN lang=EN>
<P dir=ltr align=left>The BigSpeak Audio Health Dashboard enables Text To Speech (TTS) to notify operators of the current health status of their Bigfix environment.<BR>This example only provides part of the ‘BES Relay Health’ section of the ‘Deployment Health Checks’ dashboard, However you could build out the rest of the dashboard, or utilize this example in a whole different way.</P>
<P dir=ltr align=left>The Checks that this example will report on are:</P>
<UL>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>Number of Clients Per BES Relay
<LI>BES Relay Version
<LI>BES Relay Service Stopped
<LI>Download Folders
<LI>BES Relay Free Disk Space
<P></P></LI></UL>
<P dir=ltr align=left>Every hour (by default), the native windows TTS engine will inform you as follows:</P>
<P dir=ltr align=left>"This is a Bigfix Audio Alert"</P>
<UL>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>If all 5 health checks pass, you will hear, "The current Bigfix status is ALL CLEAR"
<P></P>
<P dir=ltr align=left></P>
<LI>If one or more of the 5 checks FAIL, you will hear a combination of the following:
<P></P></LI></UL>
<DIR>
<DIR>
<P dir=ltr align=left>"The current Bigfix status for Number of Clients Per Relay is FAIL"<BR>"The current Bigfix status for Relay Version is WARNING"<BR>"The current Bigfix status for Relay Version is FAIL"<BR>"The current Bigfix status for Relay Service Stopped is FAIL"<BR>"The current Bigfix status for Download Folders is FAIL"<BR>"The current Bigfix status for Relay Disk Space is FAIL"<BR></P></DIR></DIR>
<P style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr align=left><STRONG>There are two tasks which are needed:</STRONG></P>
<OL>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>BigSpeakAudio Health Dashboard Scheduled Task Setup v1.0
<LI>BigSpeak Audio Health Dashboard
<P style="MARGIN-RIGHT: 0px" dir=ltr align=left>&nbsp;</P></LI></OL><B>
<P dir=ltr align=left>Initial Setup:</P></B>
<P dir=ltr align=left>Note: This has only been tested on Windows 7.</P>
<OL>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>Copy the ‘IEM CLI’ folder from your Bigfix server to a location on your windows 7 machine. The default location is: <I>C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Server\IEM CLI
<P></P></I>
<P dir=ltr align=left></P>
<LI>Since this is the first time utilizing the IEM CLI, you will have to manually authenticate from the Windows 7 endpoint in order to trust the security certificate.
<P></P>
<OL type=a>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>From the windows command line browse to the iem.exe and type, "iem login"
<LI>You will have to provide your operator credentials, then it will ask you to trust the certificate.</LI></OL></LI></OL>
<P><B>Deploy: BigSpeak Audio Health Dashboard Scheduled Task Setup v1.0</P>
<OL></B>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>On the ‘Description’ Tab, this task will ask for the following:
<OL>
<LI>The IEM Server Operator Name
<LI>The IEM Server Operator Password
<LI>The windows account name that will be used to execute the scheduled task
<LI>The windows account password that will be used to execute the scheduled task<BR></LI></OL>
<P></P>
<P dir=ltr align=left></P>
<LI>Two action parameters will also ask for input:
<OL>
<LI>The path to the IEM Command Line
<LI>The IP Address or hostname of the Bigfix Reporting Server</SPAN><SPAN lang=EN><BR></LI></OL>
<P></P>
<P dir=ltr align=left></P>
<LI>Target the Windows 7 endpoint(s) that will be using TTS to notify the operator<BR>
<P></P>
<P dir=ltr align=left></P>
<LI>Upon completion, the scheduled task "BFAudio_HealthCheck" will have been created that will run every hour by default.</LI></OL>
<P><B>Deploy: BigSpeak Audio Health Dashboard (This Task)</P>
<OL></B>
<P dir=ltr align=left>
<LI>Target the Windows 7 endpoint(s) that will be using TTS to notify the operator
<OL>
<LI>Note: Speakers must be turned on for this to work.</LI></OL>
<P></P></LI></OL>
<P><STRONG><EM>NOTE: This task will run as a policy. It will become relevant when the file ‘bread.crumb’ exist which is created by the scheduled taks every hour.</EM></STRONG></P></SPAN>]]></Description>
    <Relevance><![CDATA[version of client >= "9.0"]]></Relevance>
    <Relevance>(name of operating system starts with &quot;Win&quot;)</Relevance>
    <Relevance>exist file &quot;c:\BFAudio\Bread.Crumb&quot;</Relevance>
    <Category>IEM Maintenance</Category>
    <Source>mike.english@us.ibm.com</Source>
    <SourceReleaseDate>2015-09-29</SourceReleaseDate>
    <MIMEField>
      <Name>x-fixlet-modification-time</Name>
      <Value>Tue, 29 Sep 2015 11:14:57 +0000</Value>
    </MIMEField>
    <Domain>BES </Domain>
    <DefaultAction ID="Action1">
      <Description>
        <PreLink>Click </PreLink>
        <Link>here</Link>
        <PostLink> to deploy this action.</PostLink>
      </Description>
      <ActionScript MIMEType="application/x-Fixlet-Windows-Shell"><![CDATA[if {exist file "c:\BFAudio\Bread.Crumb"}
	delete __appendfile
	appendfile {concatenation "%0d%0a" of (preceding texts of firsts "</Answer>" of (following texts of firsts "<Answer type=%22string%22>" of (lines of files whose (last 3 of name of it = "txt") of folder "c:\BFAudio")))}
	delete "C:\BFAudio\BFAudio.tts"
	copy __appendfile "c:\BFAudio\BFAudio.tts"
	delete "C:\BFAudio\Bread.Crumb"
endif

delete __createfile
delete "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs"
createfile until TTS
'tts.vbs
set t = CreateObject("SAPI.SpVoice")
t.Speak Wscript.Arguments(0), 3
t.WaitUntilDone(4500)
TTS
move __createfile "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs"

if {exist file "c:\BFAudio\BFAudio.tts"}
wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "This is a bigfix audio alert"
//ALL CLEAR
	 if {not disjunction of (it contains ":WARN" OR it contains ":FAIL") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status is,,all clear"
	 endif
//Number of Clients Per BES Relay
	 if {disjunction of (it contains "Number of Clients Per BES Relay" AND it contains ":FAIL") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status for, Number of Clients Per Relay is,,FAIL"
	 endif
//BES Relay Version
	 if {disjunction of (it contains "BES Relay Version" AND it contains ":WARN") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status for, Relay Versions is,,WARNING"
	 elseif {disjunction of (it contains "BES Relay Version" AND it contains ":FAIL") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status for, Relay Versions is,,FAIL"
	 endif
//BES Relay Service Stopped
	 if {disjunction of (it contains "BES Relay Service Stopped" AND it contains ":FAIL") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status for, Relay Service Stopped is,,FAIL"
	 endif
//Download Folders
	 if {disjunction of (it contains "Download Folders" AND it contains ":FAIL") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status for, Download Folders is,,FAIL"
	 endif
//BES Relay Free Disk Space
	 if {disjunction of (it contains "BES Relay Free Disk Space" AND it contains ":FAIL") of lines of file "c:\BFAudio\bfaudio.tts"}
		wait "C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\CustomSite_BIGTWEET\RunAsCurrentUser.exe" --w --q cmd.exe /C cscript "c:\BFAudio\tts.vbs" "The current bigfix status for, Relay Disk Space is,,FAIL"
	 endif

endif]]></ActionScript>
    </DefaultAction>
  </Fixlet>
</BES>
